gs Henderson, and regional musicians. This report documents the festival and lineup; it does not establish the complete production credits.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-13", "date": "2008-06-12", "title": "Bricktown’s 13th annual blues festival", "publisher": "Oklahoma Gazette", "categories": ["festivals"], "type": "Festival preview", "url": "https://www.okgazette.com/news/annual-bricktown-blues-event-presents-13th-annual-festival-2955848/", "summary": "Jake Dalton previews the free Blues & BBQ event at Sheridan and Oklahoma avenues, featuring Marcia Ball, Bugs Henderson, and regional musicians. This report documents the festival and lineup; it does not establish the complete production credits.", "context": "", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-14", "title": "Bricktown Comprehensive Parking Strategy", "publisher": "City of Oklahoma City", "author": "", "date_label": "2008-07-23", "date_sort": "2008-07-23", "source_url": "https://www.okc.gov/files/assets/city/v/1/planning/plans-amp-studies/bt-parking-study072308.pdf", "categories": ["business", "records"], "article_type": "Official planning record", "summary": "The city’s parking study lists Jim Brewer among consulted stakeholders and Bricktown Parking Investors among contacted operators. It documents district parking conditions; it does not by itself establish the relationship between every similarly named parking business.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-14", "date": "2008-07-23", "title": "Bricktown Comprehensive Parking Strategy", "publisher": "City of Oklahoma City", "categories": ["business", "records"], "type": "Official planning record", "url": "https://www.okc.gov/files/assets/city/v/1/planning/plans-amp-studies/bt-parking-study072308.pdf", "summary": "The city’s parking study lists Jim Brewer among consulted stakeholders and Bricktown Parking Investors among contacted operators. It documents district parking conditions; it does not by itself establish the relationship between every similarly named parking business.", "context": "", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-15", "title": "Bricktown pioneer Jim Brewer dies", "publisher": "The Journal Record", "author": "", "date_label": "2008-11-12", "date_sort": "2008-11-12", "source_url": "https://journalrecord.com/2008/11/12/bricktown-pioneer-jim-brewer-dies/", "categories": ["remembrance", "business"], "article_type": "News report", "summary": "Remembers Jim Brewer’s investments, venues, festivals, and prominent role in Bricktown. Alongside tributes, the account describes a strong personality and disagreements with others involved in the district.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-15", "date": "2008-11-12", "title": "Bricktown pioneer Jim Brewer dies", "publisher": "The Journal Record", "categories": ["remembrance", "business"], "type": "News report", "url": "https://journalrecord.com/2008/11/12/bricktown-pioneer-jim-brewer-dies/", "summary": "Remembers Jim Brewer’s investments, venues, festivals, and prominent role in Bricktown. Alongside tributes, the account describes a strong personality and disagreements with others involved in the district.", "context": "", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-16", "title": "Jim Brewer obituary", "publisher": "The Oklahoman / Legacy", "author": "", "date_label": "2008-11-12", "date_sort": "2008-11-12", "source_url": "https://www.legacy.com/us/obituaries/oklahoman/name/jim-brewer-obituary?id=12737054", "categories": ["remembrance"], "article_type": "Family remembrance", "summary": "The family obituary recounts Jim’s early businesses, oil ventures, and work in Bricktown. Originally published November 12–13, 2008, it provides a family remembrance alongside independent newspaper coverage.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-16", "date": "2008-11-12", "title": "Jim Brewer obituary", "publisher": "The Oklahoman / Legacy", "categories": ["remembrance"], "type": "Family remembrance", "url": "https://www.legacy.com/us/obituaries/oklahoman/name/jim-brewer-obituary?id=12737054", "summary": "The family obituary recounts Jim’s early businesses, oil ventures, and work in Bricktown. Originally published November 12–13, 2008, it provides a family remembrance alongside independent newspaper coverage.", "context": "", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-17", "title": "Bricktown merchant mourns district pioneer", "publisher": "Oklahoma Gazette", "author": "", "date_label": "2008-11-14", "date_sort": "2008-11-14", "source_url": "https://www.okgazette.com/news/bricktown-merchant-mourns-death-of-districts-pioneer-2963555/", "categories": ["remembrance", "festivals"], "article_type": "News report", "summary": "Scott Cooper records Jim Cowan’s memories of Brewer, the merchants’ association, and major crowds at the 1999 Fourth of July celebration. It connects the events to Bricktown’s changing fortunes.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-17", "date": "2008-11-14", "title": "Bricktown merchant mourns district pioneer", "publisher": "Oklahoma Gazette", "categories": ["remembrance", "festivals"], "type": "News report", "url": "https://www.okgazette.com/news/bricktown-merchant-mourns-death-of-districts-pioneer-2963555/", "summary": "Scott Cooper records Jim Cowan’s memories of Brewer, the merchants’ association, and major crowds at the 1999 Fourth of July celebration. It connects the events to Bricktown’s changing fortunes.", "context": "", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-18", "title": "“Mayor of Bricktown” dies", "publisher": "Oklahoma Gazette", "author": "", "date_label": "2008-11-20", "date_sort": "2008-11-20", "source_url": "https://www.okgazette.com/news/mayor-of-bricktown-dies-2956582/", "categories": ["remembrance"], "article_type": "News report", "summary": "A remembrance of Jim Brewer’s business career and the entertainment ventures that helped bring visitors into the warehouse district.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-18", "date": "2008-11-20", "title": "“Mayor of Bricktown” dies", "publisher": "Oklahoma Gazette", "categories": ["remembrance"], "type": "News report", "url": "https://www.okgazette.com/news/mayor-of-bricktown-dies-2956582/", "summary": "A remembrance of Jim Brewer’s business career and the entertainment ventures that helped bring visitors into the warehouse district.", "context": "", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-19", "title": "Coca-Cola Bricktown Events Center directory entry", "publisher": "Billboard / World Radio History", "author": "", "date_label": "2008", "date_sort": "2008", "source_url": "https://www.worldradiohistory.com/Archive-All-Music/Billboard/00s/2008/Billboard-2008-Audarena-Venue-Guide.pdf", "categories": ["business", "records"], "article_type": "Industry directory", "summary": "The 2008 venue guide lists Brewer Entertainment with the Coca-Cola Bricktown Events Center at 425 California. This contemporaneous industry record helps document the venue’s earlier name.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-19", "date": "2008", "title": "Coca-Cola Bricktown Events Center directory entry", "publisher": "Billboard / World Radio History", "categories": ["business", "records"], "type": "Industry directory", "url": "https://www.worldradiohistory.com/Archive-All-Music/Billboard/00s/2008/Billboard-2008-Audarena-Venue-Guide.pdf", "summary": "The 2008 venue guide lists Brewer Entertainment with the Coca-Cola Bricktown Events Center at 425 California. This contemporaneous industry record helps document the venue’s earlier name.", "context": "", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-20", "title": "Bricktown merchants hold talks on future", "publisher": "The Oklahoman / Greater OKC Chamber", "author": "Steve Lackmeyer", "date_label": "2009-04-16", "date_sort": "2009-04-16", "source_url": "https://www.greateroklahomacity.com/news/2009/04/16/the-oklahoman/bricktown-merchants-hold-talks-on-future/", "categories": ["business", "remembrance", "lackmeyer"], "article_type": "Republished news report", "summary": "A Chamber-hosted newspaper report covers merchants’ discussions about Bricktown’s next phase, including plans to honor early contributors such as Neal Horton and Jim Brewer.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-20", "date": "2009-04-16", "title": "Bricktown merchants hold talks on future", "publisher": "The Oklahoman / Greater OKC Chamber", "categories": ["business", "remembrance", "lackmeyer"], "type": "Republished news report", "url": "https://www.greateroklahomacity.com/news/2009/04/16/the-oklahoman/bricktown-merchants-hold-talks-on-future/", "summary": "A Chamber-hosted newspaper report covers merchants’ discussions about Bricktown’s next phase, including plans to honor early contributors such as Neal Horton and Jim Brewer.", "context": "", "author": "Steve Lackmeyer", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-21", "title": "Alea London v. Canal Club", "publisher": "Oklahoma Court of Civil Appeals / Justia", "author": "", "date_label": "2009-10-23", "date_sort": "2009-10-23", "source_url": "https://law.justia.com/cases/oklahoma/court-of-appeals-civil/2009/458265.html", "categories": ["disputes", "records"], "article_type": "Court opinion", "summary": "An insurance-coverage appeal arising from an intoxicated-driver injury case. The opinion records that claims against Brewer Entertainment and Bricktown Canal Properties were dismissed without prejudice before the underlying trial.", "source_note": "The appeal concerned coverage for a judgment against Canal Club, not a liability finding against the Brewer companies. The appellate court reversed and remanded for judgment in the insurer’s favor. Dismissal without prejudice is not a decision on the merits.", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-21", "date": "2009-10-23", "title": "Alea London v. Canal Club", "publisher": "Oklahoma Court of Civil Appeals / Justia", "categories": ["disputes", "records"], "type": "Court opinion", "url": "https://law.justia.com/cases/oklahoma/court-of-appeals-civil/2009/458265.html", "summary": "An insurance-coverage appeal arising from an intoxicated-driver injury case. The opinion records that claims against Brewer Entertainment and Bricktown Canal Properties were dismissed without prejudice before the underlying trial.", "context": "The appeal concerned coverage for a judgment against Canal Club, not a liability finding against the Brewer companies. The appellate court reversed and remanded for judgment in the insurer’s favor. Dismissal without prejudice is not a decision on the merits.", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-22", "title": "Santa Fe Station’s hidden architecture", "publisher": "Oklahoma Gazette", "author": "", "date_label": "2010-02", "date_sort": "2010-02", "source_url": "https://www.okgazette.com/news/secret-architecture-makes-santa-fe-station-possible-as-oklahoma-citys-downtown-transportation-hub-2963840/", "categories": ["business"], "article_type": "Feature", "summary": "Ben Fenwick examines a long-hidden tunnel beneath the tracks and the station’s potential as a transportation hub. Brent Brewer discusses the building as city planning work continues.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-22", "date": "2010-02", "title": "Santa Fe Station’s hidden architecture", "publisher": "Oklahoma Gazette", "categories": ["business"], "type": "Feature", "url": "https://www.okgazette.com/news/secret-architecture-makes-santa-fe-station-possible-as-oklahoma-citys-downtown-transportation-hub-2963840/", "summary": "Ben Fenwick examines a long-hidden tunnel beneath the tracks and the station’s potential as a transportation hu