Lindsey Johnson explores Oklahoma City’s urban renewal and MAPS-era development. Jim Brewer’s entertainment investments appear within the larger story of downtown’s transformation.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-24", "date": "2012-03-22", "title": "The Rising", "publisher": "Oklahoma Magazine", "categories": ["business"], "type": "Historical feature", "url": "https://okmag.com/blog/the_rising/", "summary": "Lindsey Johnson explores Oklahoma City’s urban renewal and MAPS-era development. Jim Brewer’s entertainment investments appear within the larger story of downtown’s transformation.", "context": "", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-25", "title": "Western World Insurance v. Markel American Insurance", "publisher": "U.S. Court of Appeals, Tenth Circuit / Justia", "author": "", "date_label": "2012-05-08", "date_sort": "2012-05-08", "source_url": "https://law.justia.com/cases/federal/appellate-courts/ca10/11-6107/11-6107-2012-05-08.html", "categories": ["disputes", "records"], "article_type": "Court opinion", "summary": "The opinion describes an employee’s fall down an elevator shaft at the Bricktown Haunted House and the resulting suit against Brewer Entertainment. The injury suit had already settled; this appeal concerned the insurers’ responsibility for costs.", "source_note": "The court reversed summary judgment for Markel and remanded. This was an insurance-allocation decision, not a new injury judgment against Brewer Entertainment.", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-25", "date": "2012-05-08", "title": "Western World Insurance v. Markel American Insurance", "publisher": "U.S. Court of Appeals, Tenth Circuit / Justia", "categories": ["disputes", "records"], "type": "Court opinion", "url": "https://law.justia.com/cases/federal/appellate-courts/ca10/11-6107/11-6107-2012-05-08.html", "summary": "The opinion describes an employee’s fall down an elevator shaft at the Bricktown Haunted House and the resulting suit against Brewer Entertainment. The injury suit had already settled; this appeal concerned the insurers’ responsibility for costs.", "context": "The court reversed summary judgment for Markel and remanded. This was an insurance-allocation decision, not a new injury judgment against Brewer Entertainment.", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-26", "title": "Bass pros and cons", "publisher": "The Journal Record", "author": "", "date_label": "2012-07-26", "date_sort": "2012-07-26", "source_url": "https://journalrecord.com/2012/07/26/bass-pros-and-cons-official-says-government-incentives-for-retail-require-caution-finance/", "categories": ["business", "disputes"], "article_type": "Policy report", "summary": "A debate over government incentives for retail development includes Brent Brewer’s support for anchor stores and cautions about public subsidies. The disagreement concerns development policy.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-26", "date": "2012-07-26", "title": "Bass pros and cons", "publisher": "The Journal Record", "categories": ["business", "disputes"], "type": "Policy report", "url": "https://journalrecord.com/2012/07/26/bass-pros-and-cons-official-says-government-incentives-for-retail-require-caution-finance/", "summary": "A debate over government incentives for retail development includes Brent Brewer’s support for anchor stores and cautions about public subsidies. The disagreement concerns development policy.", "context": "", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-27", "title": "Festival of the foods", "publisher": "Oklahoma Gazette", "author": "", "date_label": "2013-04-16", "date_sort": "2013-04-16", "source_url": "https://www.okgazette.com/food-drink/festival-of-the-foods-2946235", "categories": ["festivals"], "article_type": "Feature", "summary": "Greg Elwell’s Festival of the Arts food coverage includes Brewer Entertainment’s brisket sales. It documents food operations at the Arts Council’s festival, rather than crediting Brewer with producing the entire event.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-27", "date": "2013-04-16", "title": "Festival of the foods", "publisher": "Oklahoma Gazette", "categories": ["festivals"], "type": "Feature", "url": "https://www.okgazette.com/food-drink/festival-of-the-foods-2946235", "summary": "Greg Elwell’s Festival of the Arts food coverage includes Brewer Entertainment’s brisket sales. It documents food operations at the Arts Council’s festival, rather than crediting Brewer with producing the entire event.", "context": "", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-28", "title": "Mystery train", "publisher": "Oklahoma Gazette", "author": "", "date_label": "2013-07-23", "date_sort": "2013-07-23", "source_url": "https://www.okgazette.com/news/mystery-train-2958843/", "categories": ["business", "disputes"], "article_type": "News report", "summary": "Jerry Bohnen reports on the city’s effort to acquire the Santa Fe Depot and a sharp gap between the owner’s asking price and the city’s offer. The article captures an unresolved acquisition dispute at that time.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-28", "date": "2013-07-23", "title": "Mystery train", "publisher": "Oklahoma Gazette", "categories": ["business", "disputes"], "type": "News report", "url": "https://www.okgazette.com/news/mystery-train-2958843/", "summary": "Jerry Bohnen reports on the city’s effort to acquire the Santa Fe Depot and a sharp gap between the owner’s asking price and the city’s offer. The article captures an unresolved acquisition dispute at that time.", "context": "", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-29", "title": "Grant and valuation move transit hub forward", "publisher": "The Journal Record", "author": "", "date_label": "2013-09-06", "date_sort": "2013-09-06", "source_url": "https://journalrecord.com/2013/09/06/grant-property-valuation-move-transit-hub-forward-general-news/", "categories": ["business", "disputes"], "article_type": "News report", "summary": "A follow-up covers federal grant funding and a reported $4.5 million depot valuation in the condemnation process. This is a dated account of that process, not a statement of the final acquisition price.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-29", "date": "2013-09-06", "title": "Grant and valuation move transit hub forward", "publisher": "The Journal Record", "categories": ["business", "disputes"], "type": "News report", "url": "https://journalrecord.com/2013/09/06/grant-property-valuation-move-transit-hub-forward-general-news/", "summary": "A follow-up covers federal grant funding and a reported $4.5 million depot valuation in the condemnation process. This is a dated account of that process, not a statement of the final acquisition price.", "context": "", "status": "published"}, "status": "published"}, {"id": "article-30", "title": "The Scare is Everywhere Inside the Bricktown Haunted Warehouse", "publisher": "Brewer Entertainment / PR.com", "author": "", "date_label": "2013-10-09", "date_sort": "2013-10-09", "source_url": "https://www.pr.com/press-release/520829", "categories": ["business", "festivals", "records"], "article_type": "Company announcement", "summary": "Brewer Entertainment announces the attraction’s 28th annual season at the Pepsi Chevy Bricktown Events Center, 425 California. This company-issued release documents the venue name and advertised season.", "source_note": "", "evidence": "", "metadata": {"id": "article-30", "date": "2013-10-09", "title": "The Scare is Everywhere Inside the Bricktown Haunted Warehouse", "publisher": "Brewer Entertainment / PR.com", "categories": ["business", "festivals", "records"], "type": "Company announcement", "url": "https://www.pr.com/press-release/520829", "summary": "Brewer Entertainment announces the attraction’s 28th annual season at t